{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The probe kit, diode assortment and 220-ohm resistors fit practical tasks with my breadboards, relay and LEDs: testing connections, protecting circuits and limiting LED current.",
    "The magnet wire connects meaningfully to my ferrite cores, and the clip leads fit temporary circuit connections, even though I would not buy them all now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Magnesium ribbon and the CNC carving bit require projects I have not shown any need for; buying electronics supplies does not mean I also do chemistry or CNC carving.",
    "The extrusion brackets assume a particular construction project from my caster purchase, while the 12-inch caliper exceeds what I currently need for small electronics work."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My purchases seem to have been treated as a broad interest in workshop supplies, when the specific job each item supports matters more to me.",
    "Several test-lead sets repeat the same useful connection to my electronics projects, but choosing one versatile kit removes my immediate need for the others."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I am more likely to choose supplies that have a clear use with components I already own than tools that require a new activity or setup.",
    "A related item is not always an immediate purchase: the full spool of magnet wire would make sense only once I have a specific winding project."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my electronics prototyping interests but stretched them into unrelated workshop activities and purchases without a current purpose."
}"}
